<title>HONG KONG: HK Jan orders on hand fall seven pct yr on yr.</title>
<headline>HK Jan orders on hand fall seven pct yr on yr.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-03-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Census and Statistics Department said on Thursday January orders on hand fell seven percent in value on the year against a seven percent drop in December.</p>
<p>The following are provisional percentage changes in the value of orders on hand in January 1997 over January 1996 (* means that the comparative figure has been revised):</p>
<p>						   Jan 1997   Dec 1996</p>
<p> All industries covered in the survey    -7	   -7</p>
<p> Wearing apparel				 -5	   -1</p>
<p> Textiles					  -9	   -1*</p>
<p> Electronic Products			  -11	  -15</p>
<p> Electrical products			   -2	   +3</p>
<p> Fabricated metal products		  +10	  +17</p>
<p> Plastic products			     -21	  -12</p>
<p> Printing and publishing		     -1	  -16</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6441</p>
</text>
